course: dictionary
lesson: 1789
title: Clipping: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one job. Clipping can be a noun, a thing you can hold, or the -ing form of clip, which is an action. The words around it show which one you need. «She stuck the newspaper clipping in her scrapbook.» Here a clipping is a piece cut out of a paper.
explain: «The gardener swept up the grass clippings.» Grass clippings are the small pieces cut off the grass. The word clippings ends in -s, so there is more than one little piece. Ask yourself: what was cut, and what is the thing being talked about?
explain: «He was clipping the hedge all morning.» Here clipping is an action: he was cutting the hedge short. Clip can also mean to fasten something with a clip. Read the whole sentence and see which meaning fits.
fact: A clipping is a piece cut off something, such as an article from a newspaper or a picture from a magazine.
fact: «Grass clippings» are the small pieces of grass cut off a lawn, and they can go into the compost.
fact: «Hedge clippings», «toenail clippings» and «newspaper clipping» are all common phrases.
fact: Clipping is the -ing form of clip, so it can show an action that is happening: cutting something short, or fastening it with a clip.
fact: To tell which kind of word clipping is, check the other words in the sentence: a thing is a noun, and an action is a verb form.
exercise: «The gardener put the grass clippings in the compost bin.» What are grass clippings? | *Small pieces cut off the grass | Seeds that grow into new trees | Long green roots under the soil
exercise: «Ana glued a newspaper clipping about the school fair into her scrapbook.» What is a newspaper clipping? | A page of a book | A brand-new newspaper printed each day | A letter sent to a friend | *A piece cut out of a newspaper
exercise: «He was clipping the hedge all morning.» What does clipping mean here? | Sleeping under a tree | *Cutting something short | Reading a newspaper | Painting a picture
test: What are «toenail clippings»? | Long toes that grow in a line | Shiny nails painted bright red | *Small pieces cut off toenails | A tool used to file nails
test: In «clipping the hedge», what kind of word is clipping? | A place where hedges grow | A colour | A noun, a thing you can hold | *A verb form, showing an action
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The clipping was tucked inside his book»? | A sharp tool for the garden | Cutting hair short with scissors | A fastening that holds papers together | *A cutting from a newspaper or magazine
